folder_remove_empty NEWS -- history of user-visible changes.

User-visible highlights per release. The full per-version log is in
`ChangeLog.md`.

* Version 1.7.20260928064816 (2026-09-28)

** One entry point, and CI that cannot drift from the pins

   `./_tests` is the check entry point now (`--quick`, `--gui`); `make test` and
   `make check-gui` just call it. The window display assertion lives in one place
   (`window_checks.sh --assert-private`), and `./_check_pins --ci` fails when the
   CI workflow installs something other than the pinned tools — so `make pins`
   (part of `make final`) catches a workflow that quietly added a version. The
   release checklist starts with `./make check-all`.

* Version 1.6.20260927202851 (2026-09-27)

** One command, one list, no leftover noise

   `make check-all` runs the whole pre-push set (`final`, `check-gui`,
   `check-313`); `make check-gui` is a one-liner because
   `tests/folder_remove_empty/window_checks.sh` owns the window module list;
   `docs/checks.md` documents every target, script and hook module. The window
   tests now close the window through the program's own close path, which stops a
   run in flight and cancels the pending callbacks before the root goes away —
   the tkinter teardown warning ("main thread is not in main loop") is gone.

* Version 1.5.20260927201516 (2026-09-27)

** The wrapper carries the checks

   `make check-gui`, `make check-313` and the screenshot script no longer spell
   out the xvfb flags: `python3 -m remove_empty_folder_display --wrap` owns them,
   and `--wrap-sh SNIPPET` does the same for a pipeline. `make check-gui` now
   honours `FOLDER_REMOVE_EMPTY_GUI_DISPLAY=session`, the pre-commit hook calls
   that target instead of branching on the display itself, and the private run
   records the session display, so its "the window never went there" assertion
   really runs. `_check_pins --update` pins a verified environment in one step.

* Version 1.4.20260927194352 (2026-09-27)

** One command to move a check to a private display

   `python3 -m remove_empty_folder_display --wrap CMD...` runs CMD under
   `xvfb-run` with the markers set and hands back its exit status, so a script
   no longer copies the xvfb flags. The pre-commit window check now calls
   `make check-gui` (the same target you can run by hand), `make final` fails
   when the working interpreter drifts from the pinned tools CI installs, and
   `docs/window-display.md` names the trap that `xvfb-run` re-splits a command
   string — pass a file, not `python3 -c "..."`.

* Version 1.3.20260927191420 (2026-09-27)

** The window never takes over your screen

   The display policy got one home (`remove_empty_folder_display.py`) and a
   name to call it by from a shell script: `python3 -m remove_empty_folder_display
   --check` fails when a script would open the window on the screen you are
   working on. The suite fails too when a new script runs the program without
   `xvfb-run`, so a check cannot start flashing your desktop by accident. The
   long form is in `docs/window-display.md`, and `make check-313` repeats the
   whole check on Python 3.13 in a container, read-only, so the version-specific
   break the CI found cannot wait for a push. `_check_pins` reports dev tools
   that drift from the pins CI installs.

* Version 1.2.20260927181430 (2026-09-27)

** CI, and the first bug it caught

   The repository now checks itself on GitHub (pytest, ruff, mypy on Python
   3.13), and that first run failed: the window module could not even be
   imported on 3.13, because tkinter's `Event` is only subscriptable from 3.14
   and the annotations were evaluated at import. The module defers its
   annotations now, so the declared floor really works. `requirements-dev.txt`
   pins the tool versions, and the README links the repository, the issue forms,
   the security policy and both releases.

* Version 1.1.20260927180137 (2026-09-27)

** Contributing, screenshots and a window smoke

   `make screenshots` redraws the two window images on a private display,
   `CONTRIBUTING.md` documents the setup, the checks and the release, and the
   pre-commit hook gained a `gui` module that opens the window and refuses a
   commit when its structure drifts or a control is filled with the palette
   accent. `SECURITY.md` and issue forms are in place, and `master` is protected
   against force pushes and deletions. The release notes below describe the port
   itself.

** The Python port is complete

   Phase by phase: the packaging and the repository scripts of this project, the
   engine with its keep list and its run control, the command line and the
   terminal report, the generated man and tldr pages, the tkinter window with
   its dialogs and its history, the settings file that remembers the window, and
   the release plumbing (`make install`, `.desktop`, the standalone build).

   folder_remove_empty is now written in Python. The release brings the same
   rules as the original: the shared engine that removes empty folders deepest
   first, the terminal mode with its stdout/stderr split and its colours, and
   the tkinter window with pause, restart, the folder picker and the history
   filters. The man page and the tldr page are generated from the program, the
   window remembers its size, position and settings in a small settings file,
   and the test suite compares the port with the captured behaviour of the
   original - stream for stream and exit code for exit code.

   `make install` puts a launcher in `~/sbin`, the eight icon sizes into the
   icon theme and a `.desktop` file into the application menu.
